--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/uefi/K70DiagnosticsPkg/Drivers/K70UsbDiagDxe/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,134 @@
+# K70 UEFI USB diagnostic consumer
+
+This DXE driver installs a `UNIXNU_MENU_PLUGIN_PROTOCOL` entry in Tools. It
+consumes Qualcomm's `EFI_USB_DEVICE_PROTOCOL`; it does not supply a USB PHY,
+controller, clock, power, or UsbfnIo provider. A missing provider returns
+`EFI_NOT_FOUND`, displays the inventory, and permits returning to the menu.
+
+The driver is a new implementation. The initialization-event sequence and USB
+descriptor shape were compared with the public HakiOS `xnuloader/loader.c`
+`usb_start()` and `xnuloader/efi.h`, without importing its loader, disk,
+`write_logs`, download, or flash implementation:
+
+- <https://github.com/oosexgang/hakios-xnu-kernel>
+- reviewed loader blob: `422f9d39f5d5afc5eb4fe727dc1412c811efc99c`
+- reviewed efi.h blob: `2d35c8366ae1875232104fbf65925020d839a131`
+
+Qualcomm's supplied `QcomPkg/Include/Protocol/EFIUsbDevice.h` defines the actual
+ABI. `QcomUsbCompat.h` renames source identifiers duplicated by modern MdePkg
+headers, without changing their layouts or calling convention. Static assertions
+check the protocol and descriptor offsets used here. Qualcomm's header retains
+its Linux Foundation license. `DiagFont.h` retains its original Android Open
+Source Project BSD license. New driver and test sources use
+`BSD-2-Clause-Patent`.
+
+## Query surface
+
+VID/PID is `18d1:d00d`; the interface is `ff/42/03`, with bulk OUT `01` and IN
+`81`. The synthetic serial is `K70UEFI20261104`. It is not the handset serial.
+
+The only accepted complete, printable ASCII commands are:
+
+| Command | Response |
+| --- | --- |
+| `getvar:version` | `OKAY0.4` |
+| `getvar:product` | `OKAYvermeer` |
+| `getvar:serialno` | Synthetic serial |
+| `getvar:k70-diag` | `OKAYuefi-usb-probe-v1` |
+| `getvar:k70-hello` | Fixed HELLO text |
+| `getvar:all` | Five bounded INFO packets, followed by OKAY |
+| `getvar:k70-log` | Shared ring snapshot as INFO packets, followed by OKAY |
+
+All other commands, including download, flash, erase, boot, continue, reboot,
+set_active, and OEM commands, receive FAIL. There is no BlockIo, file, partition,
+storage-write, reboot, or OS-launch call in this driver.
+
+The log command locates `gK70LogRingTableGuid` in the EFI configuration table and
+uses `K70LogRingCopySnapshot()`. A missing, invalid, or busy ring returns FAIL.
+The snapshot is immutable while streaming and bounded by a static 64 KiB buffer.
+Each INFO packet carries at most 60 bytes. Printable ASCII and CR/LF are
+preserved; other bytes become `?`. No NUL termination is required. The driver
+does not read the ring after ExitBootServices.
+
+On the host, a read-only query can be captured with the existing fastboot tool:
+
+```powershell
+fastboot.exe -s K70UEFI20261104 getvar k70-hello 2>&1
+fastboot.exe -s K70UEFI20261104 getvar k70-log 2>&1 | Tee-Object k70-uefi-log.txt
+```
+
+These commands describe the implemented protocol. Actual enumeration and queries
+on K70 have not been validated by these source-only tests.
+
+## Scheduling, transfers, and exit
+
+Manual Tools Run is the default. Esc, Enter, or Backspace requests exit. The
+reviewable limits are 30 seconds to connect, 60 seconds idle, 5 seconds for a
+pending IN transfer, and 180 seconds total. Initial disconnected/OUT-cancelled
+events before enumeration do not themselves end a session. Transfer queue
+retries back off by 100 ms.
+
+`Send()` success means queued only. A reply or log offset advances only after a
+successful terminal completion with the expected endpoint, buffer, and exact
+byte count. All transfers use the provider's allocated DMA buffers.
+
+The dedicated K70 diagnostic profile keeps `K70_USB_DIAG_AUTOSTART=0` and its
+restricted UniXNU application enters this plugin once at `TPL_APPLICATION`
+after UI initialization; it then stays in the menu awaiting actual input.
+See `Library/DiagUniXNULib/README.md` for the exact one-shot selection policy.
+
+An optional alternative is the compiler define `K70_USB_DIAG_AUTOSTART=1`.
+It is zero by default. The ReadyToBoot callback only
+initializes state and arms a 25 ms timer; it does not run a service loop. Each
+timer invocation performs one state-machine step and handles at most four
+events. Manual Run cancels the timer and takes over that session. The driver
+does not create a second protocol instance or a second ring.
+
+This bounds work performed by the consumer. A provider call can still block
+internally, and this provider's compatibility with TPL_CALLBACK is unverified.
+Autostart also depends on the platform signaling ReadyToBoot. The profile should
+remain in its diagnostic menu while active.
+
+The current source path provides a ReadyToBoot signal:
+`SiliciumPkg/Library/BootManagerLib/BootManager.c` calls `EfiBootManagerBoot()`,
+whose current mu_basecore `MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmBoot.c`
+calls `EfiSignalEventReadyToBoot()`. This establishes the intended code path;
+the timer callback actually running on the handset remains unverified.
+
+On normal exit, pending endpoints are aborted and terminal events are drained
+for at most 250 ms. Buffers are freed only when no DMA transfer remains owned;
+then Stop is called. Unconfirmed completion or cleanup failure retains the
+buffers and disables reuse. Qualcomm's Stop contract prohibits all later
+protocol access, so even a cleanly stopped service cannot start a second session
+in the same firmware boot. Query repeatedly within the active session instead.
+
+BeforeExitBootServices cancels the timer and attempts Abort/Stop without freeing
+buffers. It cannot veto a failed provider Stop. The regular tool exit is the
+required path before launching an OS; the event callback is only a fallback.
+No provider or Boot Services call occurs in the final ExitBootServices callback.
+
+## Integration and validation
+
+Add `K70DiagnosticsPkg/Drivers/K70UsbDiagDxe/K70UsbDiagDxe.inf` to the diagnostic
+profile's DSC/FDF, with `K70DiagnosticsPkg.dec`, `UniXNUPkg.dec`, and `QcomPkg.dec`
+on `PACKAGES_PATH`. The optional ring producer and its SerialPort bridge belong
+to the same diagnostics package. Firmware DSC/FDF integration is separate from
+this module.
+
+Run the asynchronous mock without touching hardware:
+
+```sh
+bash tests/run-host-tests.sh /tmp/k70-usb-diag-tests
+```
+
+The mock compiles the same protocol core with ASan/UBSan and checks the exact
+whitelist, write-command rejection, stale completion handling, six-packet
+`getvar:all`, full 64 KiB log streaming and sanitization, absent/busy/empty logs,
+timeouts, disconnect, short IN failure, oversized RX, and queue backoff.
+
+Both autostart settings were also compiled as AArch64 COFF with the current
+MdePkg, UniXNUPkg, QcomPkg, and shared-ring headers, using
+`-Wall -Wextra -Werror`. This checks C types, ABI assertions, and both callback
+paths. It does not establish firmware linkage, provider behavior, DMA cleanup,
+Windows driver binding, USB enumeration, or successful log retrieval on a
+physical handset.
diff --git a/package/uefi/K70DiagnosticsPkg/Drivers/K70UsbDiagDxe/tests/CoreMock.c b/package/uefi/K70DiagnosticsPkg/Drivers/K70UsbDiagDxe/tests/CoreMock.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dc41a18
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/uefi/K70DiagnosticsPkg/Drivers/K70UsbDiagDxe/tests/CoreMock.c
@@ -0,0 +1,193 @@
+/* Event-driven provider mock; it never opens a device or a USB handle.
+   SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent */
+#include "../K70UsbDiagCore.h"
+#include <assert.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+typedef struct {
+  int Result;
+  unsigned Queues, Aborts;
+  KD_BYTE Endpoint;
+  KD_SIZE Bytes;
+  KD_BYTE *Buffer;
+  KD_BYTE Rx[4096], Tx[4096];
+  int SnapshotResult;
+  KD_BYTE Log[KD_LOG_LIMIT];
+  KD_SIZE LogBytes;
+} MOCK;
+
+static int queue(void *context, KD_BYTE endpoint, KD_BYTE *buffer, KD_SIZE bytes)
+{
+  MOCK *m = context;
+  ++m->Queues;
+  assert(bytes <= KD_PACKET_BYTES);
+  assert(endpoint == KD_EP_OUT || endpoint == KD_EP_IN);
+  assert(buffer == (endpoint == KD_EP_OUT ? m->Rx : m->Tx));
+  m->Endpoint = endpoint; m->Bytes = bytes; m->Buffer = buffer;
+  return m->Result;
+}
+static void abort_transfer(void *context, KD_BYTE endpoint)
+{
+  MOCK *m = context;
+  assert(endpoint == KD_EP_OUT || endpoint == KD_EP_IN);
+  ++m->Aborts;
+}
+static int snapshot(void *context, const KD_BYTE **data, KD_SIZE *bytes)
+{
+  MOCK *m = context;
+  *data = m->Log; *bytes = m->LogBytes;
+  return m->SnapshotResult;
+}
+static void start(MOCK *m, KD_SESSION *s)
+{
+  KD_IO io;
+  memset(m, 0, sizeof(*m));
+  m->SnapshotResult = 1;
+  io.Context = m; io.Queue = queue; io.Abort = abort_transfer; io.Snapshot = snapshot;
+  KdSessionStart(s, &io, m->Rx, m->Tx, sizeof(m->Rx), 0);
+  KdSessionTick(s, 0);
+  assert(s->PendingRx && m->Endpoint == KD_EP_OUT);
+}
+static void receive(MOCK *m, KD_SESSION *s, const char *text)
+{
+  KD_SIZE n = (KD_SIZE)strlen(text);
+  assert(n <= KD_COMMAND_BYTES && s->PendingRx);
+  memcpy(m->Rx, text, n);
+  KdSessionTransfer(s, KD_EP_OUT, 1, n, m->Rx, 1);
+}
+static void complete_tx(MOCK *m, KD_SESSION *s, KD_TIME now)
+{
+  assert(s->PendingTx && m->Endpoint == KD_EP_IN);
+  KdSessionTransfer(s, KD_EP_IN, 1, m->Bytes, m->Tx, now);
+}
+static int prefix(const MOCK *m, const char *code)
+{
+  return m->Bytes >= 4 && memcmp(m->Tx, code, 4) == 0;
+}
+
+static void whitelist(void)
+{
+  static const char *allowed[] = {
+    "getvar:version", "getvar:product", "getvar:serialno",
+    "getvar:k70-diag", "getvar:k70-hello"
+  };
+  static const char *blocked[] = {
+    "download:00000010", "flash:boot", "erase:userdata", "boot", "continue",
+    "reboot", "reboot-bootloader", "set_active:a", "oem log", "oem reboot",
+    "getvar:versionx", " getvar:version", "getvar:version ", "getvar:"
+  };
+  KD_REPLY_PLAN p;
+  unsigned i;
+  for (i = 0; i < sizeof(allowed)/sizeof(allowed[0]); ++i) {
+    KdBuildReply((const KD_BYTE *)allowed[i], (KD_SIZE)strlen(allowed[i]), &p);
+    assert(p.Count == 1 && memcmp(p.Packet[0], "OKAY", 4) == 0);
+  }
+  for (i = 0; i < sizeof(blocked)/sizeof(blocked[0]); ++i) {
+    KdBuildReply((const KD_BYTE *)blocked[i], (KD_SIZE)strlen(blocked[i]), &p);
+    assert(p.Count == 1 && memcmp(p.Packet[0], "FAIL", 4) == 0);
+  }
+  KdBuildReply((const KD_BYTE *)"getvar:version\0flash:boot", 25, &p);
+  assert(memcmp(p.Packet[0], "FAIL", 4) == 0);
+  KdBuildReply(0, 0, &p);
+  assert(memcmp(p.Packet[0], "FAIL", 4) == 0);
+  KdBuildReply((const KD_BYTE *)"x", 65, &p);
+  assert(memcmp(p.Packet[0], "FAIL", 4) == 0);
+}
+
+static void completion_and_all(void)
+{
+  MOCK m; KD_SESSION s; unsigned packets = 0, before;
+  KD_TIME now = 2;
+  start(&m, &s); receive(&m, &s, "getvar:all");
+  while (!s.PendingRx) {
+    KdSessionTick(&s, now++);
+    assert(s.PendingTx);
+    assert(prefix(&m, packets < 5 ? "INFO" : "OKAY"));
+    before = m.Queues;
+    KdSessionTick(&s, now++);
+    assert(m.Queues == before); /* queued IN is not yet a completed IN */
+    KdSessionTransfer(&s, KD_EP_IN, 1, m.Bytes, m.Rx, now++);
+    assert(s.PendingTx); /* wrong/stale buffer cannot complete this TX */
+    complete_tx(&m, &s, now++);
+    ++packets;
+    if (packets == 6) {
+      KdSessionTick(&s, now++);
+      assert(s.PendingRx);
+    }
+  }
+  assert(packets == 6 && s.IgnoredCompletions == 6 && s.Commands == 1);
+  KdSessionStop(&s, KdUserExit);
+  before = m.Aborts;
+  KdSessionStop(&s, KdUserExit); KdSessionTick(&s, 100);
+  assert(m.Aborts == before && m.Aborts == 1);
+}
+
+static void log_stream(void)
+{
+  MOCK m; KD_SESSION s; KD_BYTE result[KD_LOG_LIMIT];
+  KD_SIZE i, copied = 0; unsigned packets = 0; KD_TIME now = 2;
+  start(&m, &s); m.SnapshotResult = 0; m.LogBytes = KD_LOG_LIMIT;
+  for (i = 0; i < m.LogBytes; ++i) m.Log[i] = (KD_BYTE)(i % 256);
+  receive(&m, &s, "getvar:k70-log");
+  do {
+    KdSessionTick(&s, now++);
+    assert(s.PendingTx);
+    if (prefix(&m, "INFO")) {
+      assert(m.Bytes > 4 && m.Bytes <= KD_PACKET_BYTES);
+      memcpy(result + copied, m.Tx + 4, m.Bytes - 4);
+      copied += m.Bytes - 4;
+    } else {
+      assert(prefix(&m, "OKAY") && m.Bytes == 4 && copied == m.LogBytes);
+    }
+    complete_tx(&m, &s, now++); ++packets;
+  } while (s.LogActive);
+  assert(packets > KD_MAX_PACKETS && copied == KD_LOG_LIMIT);
+  for (i = 0; i < copied; ++i) {
+    KD_BYTE expected = m.Log[i];
+    if ((expected < 32 && expected != '\r' && expected != '\n') || expected > 126) expected = '?';
+    assert(result[i] == expected);
+  }
+  KdSessionTick(&s, now); assert(s.PendingRx);
+  start(&m, &s); receive(&m, &s, "getvar:k70-log"); KdSessionTick(&s, 2);
+  assert(prefix(&m, "FAIL")); /* missing ring must never return fake HELLO */
+  start(&m, &s); m.SnapshotResult = 2; receive(&m, &s, "getvar:k70-log");
+  KdSessionTick(&s, 2); assert(prefix(&m, "FAIL"));
+  start(&m, &s); m.SnapshotResult = 0; receive(&m, &s, "getvar:k70-log");
+  KdSessionTick(&s, 2); assert(prefix(&m, "OKAY") && m.Bytes == 4);
+}
+
+static void timeouts_and_errors(void)
+{
+  MOCK m; KD_SESSION s; unsigned before;
+  start(&m, &s); KdSessionTick(&s, KD_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS);
+  assert(s.StopReason == KdConnectTimeout && m.Aborts == 1);
+  start(&m, &s); KdSessionConnection(&s, 0, 1);
+  assert(s.StopReason == KdRunning);
+  KdSessionConnection(&s, 1, 1); KdSessionTick(&s, 1 + KD_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS);
+  assert(s.StopReason == KdIdleTimeout && m.Aborts == 1);
+  start(&m, &s); receive(&m, &s, "getvar:version"); KdSessionTick(&s, 2);
+  KdSessionTick(&s, 2 + KD_TX_TIMEOUT_MS);
+  assert(s.StopReason == KdTransferTimeout && m.Aborts == 1);
+  start(&m, &s); KdSessionConnection(&s, 1, 1);
+  KdSessionConnection(&s, 1, KD_SESSION_TIMEOUT_MS - 1);
+  KdSessionTick(&s, KD_SESSION_TIMEOUT_MS); assert(s.StopReason == KdSessionTimeout);
+  start(&m, &s); KdSessionConnection(&s, 1, 1); KdSessionConnection(&s, 0, 2);
+  assert(s.StopReason == KdDisconnected && m.Aborts == 1);
+  start(&m, &s); receive(&m, &s, "getvar:version"); KdSessionTick(&s, 2);
+  KdSessionTransfer(&s, KD_EP_IN, 1, m.Bytes - 1, m.Tx, 3);
+  assert(s.StopReason == KdTransportError); /* short IN is not success */
+  start(&m, &s); KdSessionTransfer(&s, KD_EP_OUT, 1, 65, m.Rx, 1);
+  assert(s.StopReason == KdTransportError);
+  start(&m, &s); KdSessionTransfer(&s, KD_EP_OUT, 0, 0, m.Rx, 1);
+  m.Result = KD_QUEUE_RETRY; KdSessionTick(&s, 2); before = m.Queues;
+  KdSessionTick(&s, 50); assert(m.Queues == before && !s.PendingRx);
+  m.Result = KD_QUEUE_OK; KdSessionTick(&s, 102); assert(s.PendingRx);
+}
+
+int main(void)
+{
+  whitelist(); completion_and_all(); log_stream(); timeouts_and_errors();
+  puts("K70 USB core: whitelist, async completion, 64KiB log, timeouts PASS");
+  return 0;
+}
