diff --git a/package/uefi/K70DiagnosticsPkg/Library/K70PlatformPeiLib/README.md b/package/uefi/K70DiagnosticsPkg/Library/K70PlatformPeiLib/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7efd84d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/uefi/K70DiagnosticsPkg/Library/K70PlatformPeiLib/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+# Guarded K70 PlatformPeiLib copy
+
+This library is copied from `QcomPkg/Library/PlatformPeiLib` in
+`yyx2025/uefi-vermeer` commit `ae57e93f0eb6b556f1bb964ffb12f0e78aaaf33c`.
+The baseline source and platform/profile files are not changed here. Existing
+copyright notices and licenses on copied files remain applicable; the upstream
+root license is retained as `LICENSE.upstream` for originally unmarked files.
+
+The changed scanner and FV-list producer prevent unchecked OEM pointers from
+reaching DXE. They do not supply a Scheduler or initialize the OEM DTB service.
+Both must actually survive from the prior stage.
+
+## Guards before publishing HOBs
+
+- Use the unique MemoryMapLib `FD Reserved`/`FD_Reserved` descriptor. It must be
+  mapped executable RAM retained from OEM, at most 4 MiB, with no overlap with
+  the replacement FD. No physical candidate address is hardcoded.
+- Read only bounded 4-byte instructions. Candidate functions have a 1024-byte
+  maximum, must end in RET within the retained region, and contain at most 64
+  adjacent ADRP/ADD pairs. ADD must use the immediately preceding ADRP register.
+  Interleaved address construction and unsupported instruction forms are
+  deliberately rejected. GUID reads require 16 retained, aligned bytes.
+- A recognized registration must identify exactly one valid interface. Different
+  candidates for the same HOB GUID are rejected; error results clear outputs.
+- The matched OEM Scheduler is version `0x1000B` (1.11). The published
+  `EFIKernelInterface.h` supplies its known `0x60` prefix, WDog at `0x48` and Lock
+  at `0x58`; unknown later fields are not interpreted. `SchedulerTemplate.h`
+  binds that exact version, top-level pointers, known subtable/function prefix,
+  producer and HOB GUID to the same original TE relocation relation. Other
+  versions are rejected. The original five NULL Spinlock slots and NULL MpCpu
+  slot 6 are permitted; non-NULL replacements must still point into retained TE
+  code. Deprecated Thread slots must remain NULL. WDog and Lock methods are
+  mandatory. No missing interface is supplied or simulated.
+- DTB extension is checked against metadata derived from the matching
+  OS2.0.218.0.VNKCNXM OEM SEC TE: version `0x10001`, size `0x108`, and 32 function
+  pointers. All pointers must obey the same table-relative relocation relation
+  as the source template and point inside the retained same-TE text span. The
+  registration producer and its HOB GUID must have the verified relative
+  distances to the table. `DtbTemplate.h` contains relative metadata and input
+  hashes, with no runtime physical address or OEM instruction bytes.
+- Read the demonstrated live DTB pointer cell at interface-relative `+0x75C0`
+  only after range checking. There is no assumed size global at `+0x75C8`.
+  The blob must lie wholly in retained FD memory or the unique reserved,
+  non-device `XBL DT`/`XBL_DT` region. Check its big-endian FDT header, total size,
+  block bounds and version before using the pinned FdtLib. Require a bounded
+  `/sw/boot/config` property of at least 12 bytes, as the OEM initializer does.
+
+Static template discovery alone is insufficient: OEM code publishes this HOB
+only after its initializer succeeds. A NULL live pointer, inaccessible blob,
+missing boot config, unsupported version, or ambiguous candidate stops PEI with
+an explicit log. Returning an error must prevent DXE dispatch; the current SEC
+caller has this error-return guard. SEC output still uses the original
+framebuffer serial library, not the later DXE RAM ring.
+
+## FV-list layout and lifetime
+
+The OEM allocation is `0x250` (592) bytes: Count at `0`, eight entries starting
+at `8` with stride `0x48`, locks at `0x18 + i*0x48`, and occupancy bytes at
+`0x248..0x24f`. All arithmetic uses byte pointers. Compile-time and runtime
+bounds checks protect the lock writes. Validate Scheduler and Lock methods
+before invoking InitLock. On failure, destroy only previously successful locks
+and free the allocation. A failed InitLock does not convey a defined handle.
+Check GUID-HOB allocation results. Partial HOB creation cannot be rolled back;
+the SEC error guard must stop before any consumer uses the aborted pointers.
+
+## Limits and validation
+
+These checks establish bounded structural consistency and retained mappings.
+They cannot prove that inherited scheduler stacks, interrupts, watchdog state,
+security permissions or other OEM globals remain operational after custom SEC
+initialization. Calling a structurally valid OEM function may still fail. No
+claim of USB enumeration, successful OEM execution or XNU execution follows.
+
+Run `Tests/run-host-tests.py --uefi <pinned-source> --result <local-result.json>`.
+The scanner tests compile the actual implementation against real EDK2 headers
+and the bundled libfdt with ASan/UBSan. The separate FV-list test mocks only the
+outer Scheduler validator and lock methods so it can execute the actual list
+allocation/layout/cleanup code without invoking OEM firmware. AArch64 COFF
+syntax checks cover the changed source. These are offline tests, not hardware
+validation or a substitute for the final full EDK2 build.
