@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# USB diagnostic firmware build
+
+`build-firmware.py` is a Linux/WSL entry point for the isolated Redmi K70
+diagnostic profile. It requires Python 3.11 or newer. It does not contain an SDK.
+
+First use the project's existing firmware assembly workflow to prepare the
+pinned Mu-Silicium checkout, EDK2/Mu BaseCore feed with built BaseTools, and
+assembled UniXNU firmware tree. Older checkouts need this assembly step too.
+Initialize the project's required submodules and prepare the matching OEM
+binary inputs using [prepare-oem.py](README.md). This script does not download
+dependencies, reset feeds, assemble the tree, or prepare replacement binaries.
+
+Check the inputs without starting EDK or writing files:
+
+```sh
+python3 package/uefi/K70DiagnosticsPkg/Tools/build-firmware.py \
+  --uefi-root /path/to/mu-silicium \
+  --edk2-root /path/to/assembled/mu-basecore \
+  --tree /path/to/assembled/firmware/tree \
+  --clang-bin /path/to/compatible/llvm/bin \
+  --log /path/to/build-logs/usb-diag-01.log \
+  --check-only
+```
+
+Remove `--check-only` to build. `--device-root` defaults to this device
+repository, inferred from the installed Tools path. `--clang-bin` can instead
+come from `CLANG_BIN`. `--jobs` defaults to 2. All package paths are resolved
+from `board.toml` `[firmware].packages`, with `{uefi}`, `{edk2}`, and `{tree}`
+substitutions; the device's `package/uefi` directory is placed first.
+
+The profile is fixed to AARCH64, DEBUG, CLANGPDB, FD base `0xa7100000`, FD size
+`0x300000`, and the diagnostic defines recorded in the script. Its output is
+`Build/vermeerUsbDiag/DEBUG_CLANGPDB/FV/SILICIUM_UEFI.fd` under `--uefi-root`.
+It creates a separate `<log>.conf` directory from BaseTools templates and a
+`<log>.result.json` record. Existing logs and unowned CONF directories are
+refused. Baseline configuration and output directories are not selected.
+
+The board's firmware patches, including `Gic-Spurious.patch`, are checked
+before application. Only patches applied by this invocation are reversed in
+`finally`; target bytes must match their pre-apply snapshots afterward.
+Patch cleanup failure makes the build fail and is recorded in the result.
+An externally applied patch is refused rather than silently removed.
+An exclusive SDK patch lock serializes invocations of this entry point.
+
+No USB, partition, or flashing action is performed. A successful build still
+requires the full FD audit and device diagnostics before a hardware result can
+be claimed.
